JOIN Problem-Solving Framework:-
When you see a JOIN question, use this:

Step 1 — What columns do I need?

Example:
student name
exam score

Step 2 — Which tables contain them?
name  → students
score → exam_scores

Step 3 — How are they related?
students.student_id = exam_scores.student_id

Step 4 — Which JOIN?
Ask:
Do I need unmatched records?
If no:
INNER JOIN
If:
"show all students, even those without exams"
LEFT JOIN

Step 5 — Do I need filtering?
WHERE

Step 6 — Do I need one result per group?
GROUP BY

Step 7 — Do I need to filter groups?
HAVING
